  "body": "## Summary\n\nResolve DynamicEmb keys after receiver completion and reuse TorchRec forward while retaining DynamicEmb optimizer/state ownership. **This remains the integrated reference Draft; small review units are linked below.** Original 8518edd is preserved in merge history.\n\n## Problem\n\n459 requires receiver resolution, correct replacement/state handling and eventual backend coverage. The original integrated diff was difficult to review. Current main also adds548 FP8/gradient/offset behavior and 557 refusal/counter semantics that must be preserved.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Preserve native/split-fused completion, original-key output context and explicit slot/physical/compact identity.\n- Keep leases through final backward/cancellation and coherent full-row Storage publication.\n- Decode FP8 embedding values without converting optimizer bytes; retain current gradient precision/offsets.\n- Preserve raw/FIFO gather where receiver resolution is absent; separately fix dirty-cache/refused-insert recovery.\n\n## Scope / Out of Scope\n\nReview independent [559](https://github.com/NVIDIA/recsys-examples/pull/559), [560](https://github.com/NVIDIA/recsys-examples/pull/560), [563](https://github.com/NVIDIA/recsys-examples/pull/563) and [562](https://github.com/NVIDIA/recsys-examples/pull/562), then the [HBM/backend/layout previews](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PR_REVIEW_GUIDE.md). Cache has an actual HBM+563 prerequisite base; raw compatibility is independent of extra layouts. 557 supersedes558.\n\nThis source is integrated with main 2995c41; the earlier semantic conflict is resolved. Historical raw JSON is outside feature diffs and preserved at immutable8518 links/archives. Real fabric/network PS and complete version/application combinations remain outside local validation.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Evidence | Actual result |\n|---|---|\n| Current 551 reference corpus |865 passed,6 skipped per rank |\n| Independent lifetime / adapter / refusal repair |92 (+3 separate two-device cases) /306 /11 passed |\n| Prefix HBM / Cache / Storage / pooled |67 /130 /219 /268 passed per rank; exact commits in matrix |\n| TW-RW / hierarchy |2-GPU parity+jagged and 4-GPU gradient /5 contract cases; no actual NVLink/GIN |\n| Earlier same-session table / FP8 / new-upstream |409 passed,4 skipped /18 /36; not relabeled final-head reruns |\n\nTwo fresh35-unit native builds plus fatbins use SM120, PyTorch 2.13/cu130, FBGEMM 1.8 and TorchRec v1.8.0-rc1. Current root pre-commit passes. [Commands, source hashes, skips and failures](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PR_VALIDATION_MATRIX.md) distinguish every run; no external CI/container pass is inferred.\n\n## Performance\n\nIsolated raw compatibility improves raw 11\u201312.7%, Host 5.4\u20136.7%, Hybrid 3.7\u20134.1%. Measured functional24116cad80 still trails main:1.846\u21922.013ms raw,2.293\u21922.595ms Host,2.845\u21923.240ms Hybrid,17.034\u219217.643ms SparseDist. Small SparseDist shifts vary. The subsequent refusal-only fix has final-head correctness tests, not a fresh throughput claim. [Full evidence](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PERFORMANCE_REPORT.md) retains adverse results.\n\n## Dependencies / Follow-ups\n\nKeep Draft pending maintainer review/CI, representative performance acceptance and unavailable deployment checks. See [RFC552](https://github.com/NVIDIA/recsys-examples/issues/552) and [merge plan](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/MERGE_PLAN.md). No automatic merge, Ready transition, review request, comment or issue closure;459 remains open.\n",
